{"metabox":"1","type":"annotation","subject":"apps/clax_app/lib/clax/http_api.dart","issuer":"mailto:alex@kesling.co","issuer_type":"ai","created_at":"2026-10-12T06:22:14.697958Z","id":"fc658f2c08c0f33b60daa58a70b1a3c3f59f6ae6d41edd6d3b92a9a72c6e4bfa","body":{"detail":"test/clax/http_api_test.dart checks the request (POST /api/artifacts/<aid>/versions:restore, body {version, if_version}, no X-Clax-Session) and the parsed answer. test/clax/http_api_real_test.dart does not call it, because the route (crates/clax-server/src/routes/artifacts.rs `restore`) was not on the branch when the client landed. The macOS integration test's Restore step, or a line in http_api_real_test.dart, should exercise it against the daemon, including a stale if_version (409 conflict with current).","kind":"concern","span":{"start":{"line":123},"end":{"line":135},"content_hash":"f91e24fb1030ae468367c885b24d59bc517d77bd7a1f66b7110f8086e2d20842"},"summary":"restoreVersion is tested only against the scripted server, not the real daemon","tags":["test-gap","session:claude-code:e697d918-f48a-41f9-aac4-4be74128e8ae"]}}
{"metabox":"1","type":"annotation","subject":"apps/clax_app/lib/clax/http_api.dart","issuer":"mailto:alex@kesling.co","issuer_type":"ai","created_at":"2026-10-12T06:22:14.698043Z","id":"4720080d8cf2cee3bfbdfa71bf043182f17d07ad12f74f167a6d588df180ff09","body":{"detail":"The client and its scripted test follow the shape {collections: [{path, count}]} from docs/superpowers/specs/2026-10-12-flutter-app-design.md section 3.8. Until that route lands, the call answers 404 (ClaxApiError status 404), so a caller summarising other apps must treat a 404 as no collections. Once the route exists, add it to test/clax/http_api_real_test.dart.","kind":"concern","span":{"start":{"line":260},"end":{"line":272},"content_hash":"e309b9cb1b965dea4c1ea8254e27257e056f30f4a2d277da37b6da2c55bdbe36"},"summary":"collections() calls GET docs:collections, a route the daemon does not have yet","tags":["test-gap","session:claude-code:e697d918-f48a-41f9-aac4-4be74128e8ae"]}}
{"metabox":"1","type":"annotation","subject":"apps/clax_app/lib/clax/api.dart","issuer":"mailto:alex@kesling.co","issuer_type":"ai","created_at":"2026-10-12T06:22:14.698089Z","id":"835cbc19df61800aa57feab783aa1936d0ac0aac18f7bebe32d069cb39cfd127","body":{"detail":"POST /api/sessions/<sid>/feedback/ack accepts thread_ids or comment_ids (crates/clax-server/src/routes/feedback.rs AckBody); it has no feedback_ids field. The design's signature ackFeedback(sid, feedbackIds) is therefore ackFeedback(sid, commentIds): callers pass FeedbackItem.commentId. Acknowledging by comment rather than thread leaves a later comment on the same thread pending.","kind":"comment","span":{"start":{"line":55},"end":{"line":57},"content_hash":"b3e9499425e3a21ea94f6edd19466f855f0e28d49b9fd9f462e7cee7f3a659da"},"summary":"ackFeedback takes comment IDs, not feedback IDs","tags":["session:claude-code:e697d918-f48a-41f9-aac4-4be74128e8ae"]}}
{"metabox":"1","type":"annotation","subject":"apps/clax_app/lib/clax/http_api.dart","issuer":"mailto:alex@kesling.co","issuer_type":"ai","created_at":"2026-10-12T06:27:36.541171Z","id":"34bc319d1500749f5d3456c61057ca999de112775365ed5bb4688e0877358aa3","body":{"detail":"PUT /api/sessions/<sid>/working/<aid> (crates/clax-server/src/routes/working.rs:88-131) answers 404 not_found both for an unknown session (live(), line 19) and for an unknown artifact (st.get_artifact(&id)?.ok_or(CoreError::NotFound), line 107). setWorking wraps the call in _sessionCall (http_api.dart:393-407), which rewrites every 404 not_found to code unknown_session. An artifact the person deleted while its change was queued therefore looks like a lost session, and a worker that re-registers on unknown_session (spec 3.6) re-registers instead of dropping the change. Map 404 to unknown_session only on the routes whose sole resource is the session (pollFeedback, ackFeedback), and let setWorking's 404 stay not_found; FakeClaxApi.setWorking (fake_api.dart:403-404) already throws not_found for an unknown artifact, so the two disagree today.","kind":"concern","span":{"start":{"line":210},"end":{"line":228},"content_hash":"907b4ef775a05dfa43514008abf33d2499b9db163b6e16310bd71164d4556c5f"},"summary":"setWorking reports an unknown artifact as unknown_session","tags":["review","api-contract","session:claude-code:e697d918-f48a-41f9-aac4-4be74128e8ae"]}}
{"metabox":"1","type":"annotation","subject":"apps/clax_app/lib/clax/http_api.dart","issuer":"mailto:alex@kesling.co","issuer_type":"ai","created_at":"2026-10-12T06:27:36.541323Z","id":"0f859815dfd4694c7d09cc8102f956207cb0cc44ed5f3cededac75af37f4b8d9","body":{"detail":"POST /api/artifacts/{aid}/versions:restore is routed (crates/clax-server/src/routes/mod.rs api_slow) and implemented (crates/clax-server/src/routes/artifacts.rs:692-754). test/clax/http_api_real_test.dart already has v1 (index.html + app.js) and v2 (app.js removed); a restoreVersion(aid, 1, ifVersion: 2) there can assert v3 with label 'Restored v1', readFiles(aid, 3) equal to v1's files, a stale ifVersion as 409 conflict with current, an unknown n as 404, and the documents written later untouched. A few lines close this record with evidence.","kind":"comment","references":"fc658f2c08c0f33b60daa58a70b1a3c3f59f6ae6d41edd6d3b92a9a72c6e4bfa","span":{"start":{"line":123},"end":{"line":135},"content_hash":"f91e24fb1030ae468367c885b24d59bc517d77bd7a1f66b7110f8086e2d20842"},"summary":"The restore route is in the daemon now; the real-daemon test should cover restoreVersion","tags":["review","test-gap","session:claude-code:e697d918-f48a-41f9-aac4-4be74128e8ae"]}}
{"metabox":"1","type":"annotation","subject":"apps/clax_app/lib/clax/fake_api.dart","issuer":"mailto:alex@kesling.co","issuer_type":"ai","created_at":"2026-10-12T06:27:36.541476Z","id":"de290450a013a3c9370a437691c26f6c7ae7a2b48ddba3e316704fb8ec257977","body":{"detail":"The daemon checks X-Clax-Session on create and publish (publishing_session, crates/clax-server/src/routes/artifacts.rs:136-150) and answers 400 unknown_session when it names an ended or unknown session. FakeClaxApi.createArtifact and publish never call _liveSession, so after endSession(installId) they still succeed as the old session ID. F4b's worker must re-register on unknown_session (spec 3.6), and a test of that against the fake passes even when the loop never handles a refused publish. Check _liveSession(sessionId!) in createArtifact and publish when sessionId is set, as replyAsAgent/resolveAsAgent/setWorking already do.","kind":"concern","span":{"start":{"line":224},"end":{"line":289},"content_hash":"ab4970d9c76a65c1a87522d0457681e6f64c19eb6870317946a57bac3dd14061"},"summary":"FakeClaxApi creates and publishes as an ended session; the daemon refuses with unknown_session","tags":["review","fake-fidelity","session:claude-code:e697d918-f48a-41f9-aac4-4be74128e8ae"]}}
{"metabox":"1","type":"annotation","subject":"apps/clax_app/lib/clax/http_api.dart","issuer":"mailto:alex@kesling.co","issuer_type":"ai","created_at":"2026-10-12T06:27:36.541518Z","id":"d7ac8febd7711785f1d1b8a92aed40d8c199dc52916c30070157764f74c7ad14","body":{"detail":"With sessionId null, _send omits X-Clax-Session (line 508) and the daemon creates an artifact with no owner session: no watch, so comments sent on it reach no app session and the worker never sees them. replyAsAgent, resolveAsAgent and setWorking refuse with StateError before any request (_needSession); createArtifact and publish, the other agent calls named in api.dart:10-12, could do the same. FakeClaxApi.createArtifact (fake_api.dart:241) also accepts a null session.","kind":"suggestion","span":{"start":{"line":96},"end":{"line":120},"content_hash":"c0c8c4da13087d58e88f58d18f7be4a4e341761c3298c9b539b33581795dc873"},"summary":"createArtifact and publish without a session silently act as the owner","tags":["review","session:claude-code:e697d918-f48a-41f9-aac4-4be74128e8ae"]}}
{"metabox":"1","type":"annotation","subject":"apps/clax_app/lib/clax/http_api.dart","issuer":"mailto:alex@kesling.co","issuer_type":"ai","created_at":"2026-10-12T06:27:36.541568Z","id":"a72c87160b3c6cece93d6b41a17e63995696bf20a9c215920c7395daaebed0d4","body":{"detail":"getDoc treats every 404 as 'no document', but the daemon's missing-document 404 carries error.path (crates/clax-server/src/error.rs:46-50, DocNotFound) and a missing artifact's does not. clip (lines 230-239) likewise returns null for an unknown artifact or thread. FakeClaxApi.getDoc (fake_api.dart:490-494) and clip (412-418) throw not_found for those, so code tested against the fake meets a different answer in the app. Return null only for a 404 with body['path'] in getDoc, and align the fake with whichever rule is chosen.","kind":"suggestion","span":{"start":{"line":286},"end":{"line":295},"content_hash":"476246ba61a8b2773e2c8f4e1b5c8021cb36400581be52f0c844c6d02a7e0c80"},"summary":"getDoc and clip return null for an unknown artifact; the fake throws not_found","tags":["review","fake-fidelity","session:claude-code:e697d918-f48a-41f9-aac4-4be74128e8ae"]}}
{"metabox":"1","type":"annotation","subject":"apps/clax_app/lib/clax/fake_api.dart","issuer":"mailto:alex@kesling.co","issuer_type":"ai","created_at":"2026-10-12T06:27:36.541613Z","id":"15f533322444ee4fcc43b475886f237b640aa3a4a6a36eb23ecf13853ebcdba8","body":{"detail":"The daemon's stream always starts with event ready {resumed} (crates/clax-server/src/routes/events.rs, the ready once-stream), and HttpClaxApi.events documents ready/resync as the listener's cue to refetch (api.dart:97-101). The fake's stream yields only what emit() sends, and its data omits the type field the daemon serialises. A screen (F8) that refetches on ready behaves differently against the fake. Emit ready {resumed: false} to each new listener.","kind":"suggestion","span":{"start":{"line":523},"end":{"line":531},"content_hash":"064d5624b07482ddea552f75febe33008ab59b9b23ecbc8ac35a7e487cd8836f"},"summary":"FakeClaxApi.events never opens with ready, unlike GET /api/events","tags":["review","fake-fidelity","session:claude-code:e697d918-f48a-41f9-aac4-4be74128e8ae"]}}
{"metabox":"1","type":"annotation","subject":"apps/clax_app/lib/clax/sse.dart","issuer":"mailto:alex@kesling.co","issuer_type":"ai","created_at":"2026-10-12T06:27:36.541660Z","id":"d37c76e8d9f1b90dad1c42a4ab791ef0605f575e011dabc9f72a3b7a55373ccc","body":{"detail":"The daemon sends a ': keep-alive' comment every 15 s while idle (crates/clax-server/src/daemon.rs sse_keep_alive). reconnectingSse waits on open() and on the connection with no limit, so a connection that stops delivering bytes without closing (a frozen daemon, a socket left half-open after the app is suspended) is never replaced. A deadline of a few keep-alive periods with no bytes, and a connect timeout on open, would turn that into an ordinary reconnect with Last-Event-ID.","kind":"suggestion","span":{"start":{"line":91},"end":{"line":138},"content_hash":"431e780e8916a7bc577c1b2fe71ebe7105048d63ccf10c365618668be486add3"},"summary":"The event stream has no idle or connect deadline","tags":["review","session:claude-code:e697d918-f48a-41f9-aac4-4be74128e8ae"]}}
